---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { sources } from '../data/sources';
import { path } from '../lib/paths';
---

<Base
  title="The evidence, with the footnotes"
  description="Sources, uncertainty, and editorial principles behind deadbutt.fyi. No miracle cures, invented prevalence rates, or diagnostic quizzes."
>
  <header class="wrap page-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">The evidence / Last editorial review: October 10, 2026</p>
    <h1>
      Butt jokes.
      <br />
      <span class="serif-word">Actual footnotes.</span>
    </h1>
    <p>
      You deserve useful information without a frightening story about your body. Here’s what
      informed this guide, and where we’re keeping our claims modest.
    </p>
  </header>
  <section class="wrap intro-grid" style="padding-bottom:45px">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>How we call it.</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Established guidance:</strong> regular physical activity and strength training
        support health.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Promising, limited evidence:</strong> foot exercises and minimalist shoes may
        improve some foot-strength outcomes.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Not established here:</strong> a “dead butt epidemic,” a diagnostic self-test, a
        single posture that explains your pain, or a shoe that fixes your glutes.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="callout" style="margin-top:0">
      <p>
        <strong>A friendly independent guide.</strong> This is an educational project by{' '}
        <a href="https://crs.land">Chris Smothers</a>, not a clinical service. It has not been
        individually reviewed by a medical professional. Exercise amounts are conservative examples
        you can adjust, not prescriptions or claims from a clinical trial.
      </p>
      <p>
        No ads, affiliate links, or product sales. No accounts. Check-in answers stay in this page’s
        memory and disappear when you reload; we do not send or store them. GitHub Pages may process
        ordinary hosting access logs.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap source-list" aria-label="Source library">
    {sources.map((source, i) => (
      <article class="source-item" id={source.id}>
        <span>{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">
            {source.type} · {source.year}
          </p>
          <h2>
            <a href={source.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              {source.title} ↗
            </a>
          </h2>
          <p>
            <strong>{source.label}.</strong> {source.note}
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
    ))}
    <article class="source-item">
      <span>10</span>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Orthopaedic patient guidance</p>
        <h2>
          <a
            href="https://www.orthoinfo.org/recovery/hip-conditioning-program/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Hip conditioning program ↗
          </a>
        </h2>
        <p>
          <strong>American Academy of Orthopaedic Surgeons.</strong> Background on hip muscle groups
          and gradual conditioning. Not an endorsement of this website or its exercise sequence.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap section intro-grid pt-0">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Part of a curious little corner of the internet</p>
      <h2>
        Keep <span class="serif-word">exploring.</span>
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The invitation-first approach here owes a nod to{' '}
        <a href="https://crs48.github.io/floor-life/">Floor Life</a>,{' '}
        <a href="https://crs48.github.io/nervous-system-healing/">Nervous System Healing</a>, and
        the interactive explanations in{' '}
        <a href="https://crs48.github.io/ai-explained/">AI Explained</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Spotted a claim that needs a better source or an accessibility problem?{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/crs48/deadbutt/issues">Open an issue on GitHub</a>. Please keep
        personal health information out of public issues.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href={path('learn/')}>
        Back to the guide →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
